# Content schema

Content lives in `content/campaigns/<slug>/` as plain files, not a
database — `campaign.json`, `map.json`, and `articles/<slug>.md`
(frontmatter + markdown body). The Zod schemas in
`src/lib/content/schema.ts` are the single source of truth; always
validate through the helpers in `src/lib/content/{campaigns,articles,map}.ts`
instead of writing files by hand.

- Articles: `title`, `slug`, `tags` (array), one-sentence `summary`,
  optional `image`, and a markdown `body` kept to roughly half a page
  (`ARTICLE_WORD_LIMIT` in `schema.ts`). Link to other articles with plain
  markdown links to `/campaigns/<slug>/articles/<other-slug>` so readers
  can navigate between them.
- Map cells: integer `(x, y)` centered on `(0, 0)`, an `icon` key that must
  exist in `MAP_ICONS` (`src/lib/icons.ts`), a `label`, and a `search`
  payload (`text`/`tags`) or `articleSlug` describing what clicking the
  icon should show.
- After bulk edits, run `pnpm lint:content` to catch oversized articles or
  unknown map icons.
- Never bypass the API route handlers from client components — they own
  filesystem access and Zod validation.
